  "answers": "parity request A6 — 'psz-godot's area B uses room codes it guessed from shapes'",
  "*** AREA B'S CODES ARE AREA A'S, VERBATIM ***": "the room code carries the area in its variant field, and for all seven stages the set of room suffixes under variant 'b' is IDENTICAL to the set under variant 'a' — not similar, equal, with an empty symmetric difference in every stage. No guessing was ever needed.",
  "variant_roles": {
    "a": "area A. 16 or 17 rooms per stage.",
    "b": "area B. the same 16 or 17 rooms as that stage's area A.",
    "e": "a side area: 2 rooms (ia1, nr2) in stages 1-7, and 10 in stage 8.",
    "z": "the stage CLIMAX room, and only six of the eight hold an actual boss."
  },
  "*** STAGES 3 AND 4 HAVE NO BOSS ***": "s01z, s02z, s05z, s06z and both s07z rooms carry a boss template and run exactly one wave (w3 == w4 == 1). s03z_na1 and s04z_na1 carry none: their lists hold only three-enemy GORILLA and ARMADILLO waves respectively, and they run exactly three waves (w3 == w4 == 3). So the two kinds of climax room are separable by their own wave counts.",
